==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Li'l Giraffe Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Li'l Lion Cat''' when obtained from the [[Tiny Horns (Deadly)|Li'l Cow Awakens! Stage]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Due to being the Li'l version of a [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cat]], Li'l Cow Cat suffers from a severe lack of good basic stats, which makes this unit underperform greatly in his field. For this reason, usage of Li'l Cow Cat prior to unlocking his True Form is not recommended.

==='''True Form'''===
Li'l Lion Cat's stat buffs allow him to become a rush unit almost on par with Lion Cat and [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]]. Despite lacking the speed the others have, he makes up for it with his immunity to [[Wave Attack]]s. This allows him to rush and stall [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|wave attackers]], such as [[Kory]], [[Hermit Cat (Enemy)|Hermit Cat]], and even [[Li'l Jamiera Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Jamiera Cat]], provided he's boosted enough to handle their raw offensive output, though you may obtain better Wave Immune meatshields, notably Talented [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Mohawk Cat]] who is much cheaper and faster to produce.

==='''Talents'''===
Li'l Lion's Talents, added in [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]], are decent for what they do, albeit expensive in NP.

First and foremost, he gains up to 10% chance to destroy [[Shield]]s. While this may be good on paper thanks to his fast speed, attack cycle and immunities, including a Surge Immune talent, Li'l Lion is still not fast enough to slip in hits, has very short range and the chance is still extremely low. Even against shielded threats that create waves like [[Deathkory]], [[Wicked Face]] and [[Possessed Empress]], he will struggle to get to them in the first place due to supporting enemies. If you want a rusher with Shield Piercing, [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] is much more reliable, having a guaranteed chance to pierce shields, higher speed and damage and an extra Knockback ability on top. Despite these issues however, the Talent can be useful against [[Poultrio]] as part of a cheese strategy in [[Feathergeddon: Swan Song (Brutal)|its final stage]].

To further aid in this niche, Li'l Lion gets Cost Down, reducing his cost to 450c. Since Li'l Lion was a bit expensive for what he does, it is highly recommended to unlock it if you do need a specialist meatshield for wave and surge stages yet lack the necessary alternatives.

Finally, he gets the standard Attack and HP talents that most units receive. However, both are completely useless, as Li'l Lion is never used for his stats, which are too low to matter anyways, not to mention their extreme NP cost for what little they do.

